1
00:01:28,051 --> 00:01:33,924
THE OHARA FAMILY TREASURE

2
00:01:42,199 --> 00:01:45,068
Hey, are you sure this is the right way?

3
00:01:45,536 --> 00:01:50,908
I think so. It must be a new road, not even on the GPS.

4
00:01:51,108 --> 00:01:53,911
I haven't seen a single oncoming car for a while.

5
00:01:54,111 --> 00:01:55,612
How about you, Honda?

6
00:01:55,846 --> 00:01:58,882
If we're still on the old road, then there's no doubt.

7
00:01:59,082 --> 00:02:00,451
It's one road all the way.

8
00:02:01,051 --> 00:02:05,122
But does the chief really commute from a place like this?

9
00:02:05,589 --> 00:02:10,060
Yes, by public and private railway, bus, and then a 20-minute walk.

10
00:02:10,260 --> 00:02:11,962
It takes him about 2.5 hours.

11
00:02:12,229 --> 00:02:15,866
Jeez, a five-hour round trip! That'd drive me nuts.

12
00:02:16,233 --> 00:02:19,870
By the way, what did you buy for the chief's birthday, Ryo-chan?

13
00:02:20,504 --> 00:02:22,873
You mean this? It's a secret till we get there.

14
00:02:23,140 --> 00:02:27,878
Why? We all paid for it, so you should tell us.

15
00:02:28,178 --> 00:02:32,616
Don't worry. I chose very carefully. There's no mistake.

16
00:02:32,816 --> 00:02:39,590
It's not right if the people giving a gift don't even know what they're giving.

17
00:02:39,790 --> 00:02:40,624
That's right.

18
00:02:42,359 --> 00:02:45,796
I can only say it's a really wonderful gift.

19
00:02:46,063 --> 00:02:50,134
When the chief sees this, he'll surely be so moved he'll faint from the shock.

20
00:02:52,503 --> 00:02:55,172
Oh, we're in a residential area all of a sudden.

21
00:02:55,372 --> 00:02:57,441
We should be arriving soon.

22
00:02:57,641 --> 00:03:01,144
This is a pretty miserable-looking place.

23
00:03:08,785 --> 00:03:12,322
Ouch... Why did you do that without warning?

24
00:03:12,523 --> 00:03:15,626
Huh? Ryotsu?

25
00:03:18,395 --> 00:03:21,331
Um, I'd like to ask you something.

26
00:03:21,798 --> 00:03:22,966
Yes?

27
00:03:23,300 --> 00:03:26,403
Do you know the Ohara's house?

28
00:03:26,837 --> 00:03:30,107
Oh, it's about another kilometer ahead.

29
00:03:30,307 --> 00:03:34,978
I see. If you don't mind, please come with us to show us the way.

30
00:03:35,179 --> 00:03:36,847
We'll drop you at your house.

31
00:03:37,114 --> 00:03:40,584
There's only one road, so you won't get lost.

32
00:03:40,851 --> 00:03:44,354
Don't say that. Any journey is better with a companion, right?

33
00:03:44,555 --> 00:03:48,158
Oh dear. When he sees a pretty woman, he always acts like this.

34
00:03:49,593 --> 00:03:51,962
Get out, Honda. She's getting in.

35
00:03:52,162 --> 00:03:54,965
What am I supposed to do then?

36
00:03:55,332 --> 00:03:58,035
I heard it's just a short walk.

37
00:03:58,335 --> 00:04:00,571
Then, we don't need her to show us the way.

38
00:04:00,804 --> 00:04:04,074
Um, you don't have to give me a ride.

39
00:04:04,441 --> 00:04:07,077
Sorry, please hold on a moment.

40
00:04:07,277 --> 00:04:08,445
Hey, get out now.

41
00:04:08,679 --> 00:04:11,348
Ryotsu, this car can seat five people.

42
00:04:11,548 --> 00:04:13,917
Shut up, Nakagawa. I don't like being cramped!

43
00:04:14,151 --> 00:04:16,453
Ryo-chan, I feel sorry for Honda-san.

44
00:04:16,687 --> 00:04:18,355
Reiko, you sit in the front seat!

45
00:04:18,822 --> 00:04:22,092
Honda, don't you think it's rude to keep a lady waiting?

46
00:04:22,426 --> 00:04:24,061
B-But...

47
00:04:24,261 --> 00:04:27,097
Stop complaining and just get out!

48
00:04:27,297 --> 00:04:28,832
After you.

49
00:04:31,034 --> 00:04:33,937
Oh man, how did it come to this?

50
00:04:34,171 --> 00:04:36,940
Why does it always end up like this?

51
00:04:37,174 --> 00:04:40,377
So, you're going to celebrate your boss's birthday?

52
00:04:40,577 --> 00:04:44,181
That's right. This is what we call "social obligation."

53
00:04:44,381 --> 00:04:48,652
That's tough. You've come all the way to the mountains on your day off.

54
00:04:48,952 --> 00:04:51,121
I can't believe he built his house here.

55
00:04:51,321 --> 00:04:54,124
It looks more like a place for raccoon dogs...

56
00:04:54,324 --> 00:04:58,862
Oops, excuse me. Do you live around here too?

57
00:04:59,062 --> 00:05:01,565
Oh, yes, well...

58
00:05:01,898 --> 00:05:05,669
By the way, you must think highly of your boss to come out here

59
00:05:05,902 --> 00:05:08,105
to celebrate his birthday.

60
00:05:08,405 --> 00:05:09,473
No way!

61
00:05:09,673 --> 00:05:14,878
He's stuffy, inflexible, overbearing, yells all the time, and has smelly feet.

62
00:05:15,078 --> 00:05:18,115
Nobody thinks highly of him, that's for sure.

63
00:05:19,883 --> 00:05:23,687
I'm sorry you have to work for someone like that.

64
00:05:23,920 --> 00:05:26,423
We have to keep him happy once in a while.

65
00:05:26,957 --> 00:05:29,926
Especially since you cause him lots of trouble, Ryotsu.

66
00:05:30,127 --> 00:05:32,663
Hmph, he causes me trouble.

67
00:05:33,096 --> 00:05:34,431
There it is.

68
00:05:40,504 --> 00:05:43,507
I see. So this is the chief's house.

69
00:05:44,308 --> 00:05:49,079
A small balcony and a try-hard garden that even has a garden lantern...

70
00:05:49,279 --> 00:05:56,119
Jeez, he spent half his life grafting just to build such a tiny house.

71
00:05:57,554 --> 00:06:00,857
Oh, we have to take you home.

72
00:06:01,658 --> 00:06:03,794
That's okay. This is where I'm going too.

73
00:06:04,027 --> 00:06:05,028
Huh?

74
00:06:05,462 --> 00:06:07,531
Because this is my home.

75
00:06:07,731 --> 00:06:09,132
What?

76
00:06:09,833 --> 00:06:12,302
Does that mean, by any chance...

77
00:06:12,803 --> 00:06:15,572
Yes, I'm Hiromi, the daughter of a boss

78
00:06:15,806 --> 00:06:18,675
who is overbearing, inflexible, yells, and has smelly feet.

79
00:06:18,875 --> 00:06:20,043
Welcome, everyone.

80
00:06:20,277 --> 00:06:22,546
-Oh, you are... -The chief's...

81
00:06:22,879 --> 00:06:23,847
Yes.

82
00:06:24,047 --> 00:06:26,750
And you realized who we were earlier?

83
00:06:26,983 --> 00:06:30,854
Yes. I've heard a lot about all of you from my father.

84
00:06:31,054 --> 00:06:35,992
Well, I have always had a lot of respect for the chief

85
00:06:36,193 --> 00:06:40,497
and really think he is a model police officer.

86
00:06:40,897 --> 00:06:42,866
You don't have to force yourself.

87
00:06:43,066 --> 00:06:46,236
Because my father really is just like you said.

88
00:06:46,703 --> 00:06:48,372
Y-Yes, that's right.

89
00:06:48,605 --> 00:06:50,407
Ryotsu!

90
00:06:56,146 --> 00:06:58,014
Hey, here comes Honda.

91
00:07:00,083 --> 00:07:03,587
I'm home! Hey Dad, you have guests.

92
00:07:04,588 --> 00:07:05,555
Who could it be?

93
00:07:05,756 --> 00:07:08,158
-Oh! -Well, hello.

94
00:07:08,358 --> 00:07:10,360
What are you guys doing here?

95
00:07:10,727 --> 00:07:12,729
What's with that attitude?

96
00:07:12,929 --> 00:07:17,100
Your lovable subordinates have come all the way here to see you.

97
00:07:17,434 --> 00:07:19,703
As they say, "Great hate springs from great love."

98
00:07:19,903 --> 00:07:21,605
Oh, welcome everyone.

99
00:07:22,005 --> 00:07:25,208
We're sorry for visiting out of the blue.

100
00:07:25,408 --> 00:07:26,243
Hello.

101
00:07:27,611 --> 00:07:28,712
Well, come in.

102
00:07:29,112 --> 00:07:30,447
Excuse us.

103
00:07:30,647 --> 00:07:34,651
-Welcome. -Well, Chief, what a nice house!

104
00:07:34,885 --> 00:07:37,954
This entrance is very compact

105
00:07:38,188 --> 00:07:41,758
and perfectly represents your modest character.

106
00:07:41,958 --> 00:07:42,759
Hmm?

107
00:07:42,959 --> 00:07:45,495
And this wallpaper has a common touch

108
00:07:45,729 --> 00:07:49,466
so as not to make visitors nervous.

109
00:07:50,100 --> 00:07:51,468
You can stay outside.

110
00:07:53,069 --> 00:07:56,239
What are you saying, Dad? He came all the way here.

111
00:07:56,439 --> 00:07:57,908
Ryotsu-san, please come in.

112
00:07:59,910 --> 00:08:02,946
Who would've guessed Chief had such a pretty daughter?

113
00:08:03,146 --> 00:08:05,849
I should say, "a black kite gave birth to a swan."

114
00:08:06,082 --> 00:08:07,150
Listen up, Ryotsu.

115
00:08:07,417 --> 00:08:10,320
A word of warning. Don't get any funny ideas.

116
00:08:10,520 --> 00:08:15,459
Not that Hiromi would be interested in a rough guy like you in any case.

117
00:08:15,659 --> 00:08:19,496
I might be rough, but you're even rougher, Chief.

118
00:08:19,696 --> 00:08:20,964
How dare you!

119
00:08:21,164 --> 00:08:24,167
Stop, Dad! This isn't your office.

120
00:08:25,869 --> 00:08:26,937
Oh, I'm sorry.

121
00:08:30,340 --> 00:08:34,277
Anyway, why have you suddenly come to visit me?

122
00:08:34,778 --> 00:08:37,013
Oh, you really have no idea?

123
00:08:37,948 --> 00:08:39,015
No.

124
00:08:41,785 --> 00:08:43,787
Happy birthday, Dad!

125
00:08:44,187 --> 00:08:45,789
B-Birthday?

126
00:08:46,089 --> 00:08:47,858
Happy birthday, Chief!

127
00:08:48,124 --> 00:08:49,326
Congratulations!

128
00:08:49,526 --> 00:08:50,794
Happy birthday!

129
00:08:50,994 --> 00:08:52,796
Happy birthday, Chief.

130
00:08:53,363 --> 00:08:54,531
Here you are, Dad.

131
00:08:55,699 --> 00:08:56,733
W-What...

132
00:08:57,467 --> 00:08:59,636
Chief, say something!

133
00:09:00,871 --> 00:09:03,373
Oh, thank you, everyone.

134
00:09:05,442 --> 00:09:07,377
-Happy birthday! -Yeah!

135
00:09:10,847 --> 00:09:15,352
So, you guys came all the way here to celebrate my birthday?

136
00:09:16,586 --> 00:09:18,588
Are you crying, Chief?

137
00:09:18,822 --> 00:09:21,024
You idiot, of course not.

138
00:09:21,491 --> 00:09:24,227
Here you are, Dad. This is from me and Mom.

139
00:09:28,465 --> 00:09:30,700
Oh, leather shoes.

140
00:09:31,301 --> 00:09:33,703
I'll take good care of them.

141
00:09:33,904 --> 00:09:34,771
Chief.

142
00:09:35,372 --> 00:09:39,709
Well, this is our humble present for you.

143
00:09:40,377 --> 00:09:42,712
What's this? It's so big.

144
00:09:42,913 --> 00:09:45,582
What did Ryotsu end up buying?

145
00:09:45,782 --> 00:09:46,850
-I don't know. -Oh!

146
00:09:49,085 --> 00:09:50,687
W-What are these?

147
00:09:52,389 --> 00:09:54,925
What do you think, Chief? Takes you back, huh?

148
00:09:57,093 --> 00:10:00,564
A department store was running a nostalgic candy and toy fair.

149
00:10:00,764 --> 00:10:05,101
Look. marbles, menko, a silver bullet gun, a slingshot,

150
00:10:05,335 --> 00:10:08,772
vinegar kelp, sauce crackers, and even pickled squid.

151
00:10:08,972 --> 00:10:13,410
And these firecrackers used to be much bigger and called "2B bullets."

152
00:10:13,610 --> 00:10:17,414
Ryotsu, you used all the money we collected for these?

153
00:10:17,614 --> 00:10:21,952
Of course. I could buy quite a lot with 20,000 yen.

154
00:10:22,385 --> 00:10:24,087
You guys didn't know?

155
00:10:24,287 --> 00:10:28,291
No. Ryotsu insisted on choosing the present himself.

156
00:10:28,525 --> 00:10:31,728
I knew it was a mistake to leave it to him.

157
00:10:32,095 --> 00:10:34,197
Hey, what are these?

158
00:10:34,598 --> 00:10:36,733
Come on, don't you know menko?

159
00:10:36,933 --> 00:10:39,202
Okay, just watch.

160
00:10:39,636 --> 00:10:41,304
This is how you do it.

161
00:10:43,306 --> 00:10:45,208
It's yours if you turn it over.

162
00:10:45,408 --> 00:10:47,143
Wow, it's interesting!

163
00:10:47,377 --> 00:10:48,578
-Hmph! -Huh?

164
00:10:49,079 --> 00:10:52,315
I'll show you how to really play menko.

165
00:10:53,850 --> 00:10:55,819
You use your hips.

166
00:10:56,620 --> 00:10:58,822
I'm not gonna lose to you, Chief.

167
00:11:02,225 --> 00:11:03,827
Think you're good, huh?

168
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:12,035
How about that? Do you give up?

169
00:11:14,404 --> 00:11:15,839
Oh, I, um...

170
00:11:18,642 --> 00:11:20,310
Well, everyone.

171
00:11:21,011 --> 00:11:22,445
Thank you very much for today.

172
00:11:22,645 --> 00:11:27,684
The present aside, I'm very happy everyone celebrated my birthday.

173
00:11:28,118 --> 00:11:32,355
How can you say "the present aside"? You were really into it.

174
00:11:34,457 --> 00:11:39,863
So, as a token of my gratitude, I'd like to treat you all to tea.

175
00:11:40,497 --> 00:11:42,599
Huh, tea?

176
00:11:52,142 --> 00:11:55,545
What's this room? There's no furniture or anything.

177
00:11:55,912 --> 00:11:58,748
This is a tearoom, a place to drink tea.

178
00:11:58,982 --> 00:12:02,886
A tearoom? Good grief, the house is already small enough.

179
00:12:03,086 --> 00:12:05,055
He built a room just for drinking tea?

180
00:12:05,522 --> 00:12:08,091
Ryo-chan, you have to sit on your heels in here.

181
00:12:08,324 --> 00:12:11,761
Oh, is that right? What the heck is this?

182
00:12:13,897 --> 00:12:14,731
Hmm?

183
00:12:19,002 --> 00:12:19,836
Oh...

184
00:12:23,773 --> 00:12:24,641
Here you go.

185
00:12:25,075 --> 00:12:28,378
Thank you very much for your hospitality.

186
00:12:28,578 --> 00:12:29,779
All right then...

187
00:12:30,013 --> 00:12:31,081
Ouch! Hey!

188
00:12:31,314 --> 00:12:34,784
Don't touch them yet. Wait for the chief to come.

189
00:12:35,051 --> 00:12:36,753
Don't hit my hand!

190
00:12:38,388 --> 00:12:40,890
Please wait a moment.

191
00:12:43,426 --> 00:12:45,395
Ryo-chan, do you know how to drink tea?

192
00:12:45,595 --> 00:12:48,932
You have to turn the teacup slowly, like this.

193
00:12:49,132 --> 00:12:51,267
Sure, I know that much.

194
00:12:51,501 --> 00:12:53,536
Just spin it around three times, right?

195
00:12:53,770 --> 00:12:57,140
Don't be silly. If you turn it vertically, the tea will spill.

196
00:12:57,373 --> 00:12:58,875
Uh, ahem!

197
00:13:09,219 --> 00:13:11,254
I wonder what he's trying to show off.

198
00:13:11,788 --> 00:13:14,757
Shhh! It's already started.

199
00:13:37,380 --> 00:13:39,082
Honda-san, is something wrong?

200
00:13:39,282 --> 00:13:40,850
My legs are numb...

201
00:13:43,386 --> 00:13:44,587
Please have some sweets.

202
00:13:44,787 --> 00:13:48,124
Yes! I've been waiting for that. Finally, I got your permission.

203
00:13:48,324 --> 00:13:49,192
Okay, let's dig in.

204
00:13:52,662 --> 00:13:53,463
Ouch!

205
00:13:54,197 --> 00:13:55,965
Hey, you savage!

206
00:13:56,166 --> 00:13:57,000
What?

207
00:13:57,734 --> 00:14:00,970
You don't understand the spirit of tea at all.

208
00:14:01,171 --> 00:14:04,874
You don't have to do anything, just sit there and be quiet.

209
00:14:05,108 --> 00:14:06,442
Hmph. Got it.

210
00:14:06,776 --> 00:14:12,215
The savage aside, I want you to enjoy tea in my prized teacup.

211
00:14:12,649 --> 00:14:13,950
A teacup?

212
00:14:17,020 --> 00:14:20,523
This is my most prized possession.

213
00:14:20,990 --> 00:14:22,225
Oh my!

214
00:14:22,759 --> 00:14:26,062
I saw it while traveling in Kyoto, and I just had to have it.

215
00:14:26,296 --> 00:14:29,532
So I took the plunge, thinking I'll use it for the rest of my life.

216
00:14:29,866 --> 00:14:31,501
It's a Kuroraku-jawan.

217
00:14:31,701 --> 00:14:34,337
A fantastic piece. I think it's made by Koetsu.

218
00:14:34,804 --> 00:14:36,339
Oh, you can tell?

219
00:14:36,773 --> 00:14:38,975
The black luster is wonderful.

220
00:14:39,242 --> 00:14:42,178
Yes. I'll let you all drink tea from this teacup.

221
00:14:43,646 --> 00:14:48,184
The luster? It's just a plain, ordinary teacup.

222
00:14:48,384 --> 00:14:51,187
R-Ryotsu, hey, stop!

223
00:14:51,521 --> 00:14:53,823
Come on. Let me see it.

224
00:14:54,023 --> 00:14:54,824
Ryotsu!

225
00:15:10,039 --> 00:15:12,942
Well, Chief, that was close.

226
00:15:13,176 --> 00:15:14,577
Nice catch, Honda.

227
00:15:14,811 --> 00:15:20,083
Y-You idiot! Be careful. This teacup cost 400,000 yen!

228
00:15:20,416 --> 00:15:23,753
400,000 yen for that dingy teacup?

229
00:15:24,520 --> 00:15:29,025
In this world, there are valuable things you cannot understand.

230
00:15:29,492 --> 00:15:31,060
Jeez...

231
00:15:42,305 --> 00:15:44,574
Thank you for the lovely tea.

232
00:15:45,441 --> 00:15:47,844
What blatant flattery. Give me a break.

233
00:15:52,248 --> 00:15:54,584
Thank you for the very nice tea.

234
00:15:56,886 --> 00:15:59,155
It was very good.

235
00:16:00,323 --> 00:16:04,127
Forget about the rules. Just enjoy the tea. That's what matters.

236
00:16:04,327 --> 00:16:08,931
Well, I've made tea for three of you, so I can't leave Ryotsu out.

237
00:16:09,399 --> 00:16:12,635
Oh, Chief. I'd rather have rice soaked in tea or something.

238
00:16:13,169 --> 00:16:17,073
Hmph. That might indeed suit you better.

239
00:16:17,273 --> 00:16:20,743
But we're preparing a meal now, so hold on a little longer.

240
00:16:20,943 --> 00:16:24,080
Dad, you have a phone call.

241
00:16:24,547 --> 00:16:27,016
I see. Then Ryotsu, just wait here.

242
00:16:27,250 --> 00:16:31,087
Make sure not to touch the teacup. Okay?

243
00:16:31,421 --> 00:16:33,089
I won't.

244
00:16:38,328 --> 00:16:40,663
You'd better not.

245
00:16:42,031 --> 00:16:43,333
Gimme a break.

246
00:16:43,900 --> 00:16:45,768
What's with the 400,000-yen teacup?

247
00:16:45,969 --> 00:16:49,906
If it's so great, put a price tag on it.

248
00:16:50,106 --> 00:16:54,844
I was very nervous to drink tea from a 400,000-yen teacup.

249
00:16:55,378 --> 00:16:59,615
Tea ceremony items may look simple, but they're all valuable.

250
00:16:59,816 --> 00:17:03,286
Hmm, all this stuff?

251
00:17:03,486 --> 00:17:06,356
Oh, this'd make a good earpick.

252
00:17:06,589 --> 00:17:09,025
Ryotsu, you shouldn't do that.

253
00:17:09,225 --> 00:17:10,059
That's right.

254
00:17:10,626 --> 00:17:12,662
I don't care.

255
00:17:12,862 --> 00:17:16,833
Well, now I'll make you some tea.

256
00:17:19,035 --> 00:17:24,874
The true tea ceremony is simply stirring like a washing machine.

257
00:17:25,074 --> 00:17:27,643
Whirl and twirl! Whirl and twirl!

258
00:17:28,010 --> 00:17:29,379
Hey, stop it.

259
00:17:29,612 --> 00:17:31,848
Whirl and twirl! Whirl and twirl!

260
00:17:32,048 --> 00:17:34,350
Give me a whirl! Give me a twirl!

261
00:17:35,218 --> 00:17:38,888
Come on, Ryo-chan. Stop it already!

262
00:17:39,088 --> 00:17:40,990
Ah, whoops!

263
00:17:41,424 --> 00:17:42,258
Ryotsu!

264
00:17:44,961 --> 00:17:45,962
Ouch...

265
00:17:46,863 --> 00:17:48,064
I got a bit carried away.

266
00:17:48,264 --> 00:17:49,732
-Oh no! -What?

267
00:17:50,566 --> 00:17:52,735
-R-Ryo-chan. -Ryotsu...

268
00:17:53,069 --> 00:17:55,071
Huh? What?

269
00:18:01,844 --> 00:18:04,046
-I knew it. -You broke it.

270
00:18:04,647 --> 00:18:08,017
I can't believe it's so easy to break.

271
00:18:08,217 --> 00:18:10,353
The chief must have been scammed.

272
00:18:10,553 --> 00:18:11,521
Uh-oh!

273
00:18:11,921 --> 00:18:14,257
Sorry to keep you waiting. Hmm?

274
00:18:14,457 --> 00:18:16,025
Ryotsu, what are you doing?

275
00:18:18,094 --> 00:18:19,028
Well...

276
00:18:19,462 --> 00:18:23,533
Chief, this is really a beautiful teacup.

277
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:26,702
Do you understand how good it is?

278
00:18:27,236 --> 00:18:29,138
Of course I do.

279
00:18:29,372 --> 00:18:33,709
This texture is so wonderful I don't want to let it go.

280
00:18:34,110 --> 00:18:34,944
Really?

281
00:18:35,144 --> 00:18:38,714
Then, I'll make you tea with it, so give it back now.

282
00:18:38,915 --> 00:18:43,453
Oh, no. Let me appreciate it like this for a while longer.

283
00:18:43,853 --> 00:18:44,887
No way.

284
00:18:45,087 --> 00:18:48,057
Nothing good will happen if I let you hold it.

285
00:18:48,257 --> 00:18:49,459
Now, give it back.

286
00:18:49,892 --> 00:18:51,127
Just a little longer.

287
00:18:51,494 --> 00:18:52,295
No.

288
00:18:52,495 --> 00:18:53,930
Just a tiny bit longer.

289
00:18:54,130 --> 00:18:56,032
Come on, Ryotsu. Cut it out.

290
00:18:57,600 --> 00:18:59,235
-Hey, what's that? -Hmm?

291
00:19:01,604 --> 00:19:04,140
Hey, stop, Ryotsu. Come back here!

292
00:19:05,274 --> 00:19:06,976
Is the tea ceremony over?

293
00:19:07,176 --> 00:19:09,245
I'm preparing for the barbecue now.

294
00:19:10,113 --> 00:19:11,514
Well...

295
00:19:16,118 --> 00:19:17,453
Oh, there's a barbecue.

296
00:19:17,653 --> 00:19:19,455
It'll be ready soon.

297
00:19:19,655 --> 00:19:22,291
-Well, thank you. -Where are you, Ryotsu?

298
00:19:22,792 --> 00:19:26,262
There you are. Hey, give me back my teacup.

299
00:19:28,831 --> 00:19:29,732
Come on, Ryotsu.

300
00:19:29,932 --> 00:19:34,303
Look, Chief. This teacup looks even more beautiful in nature.

301
00:19:34,504 --> 00:19:36,305
Never mind that, just give it back.

302
00:19:36,639 --> 00:19:38,274
What's the matter?

303
00:19:38,941 --> 00:19:39,775
Well...

304
00:19:39,976 --> 00:19:42,512
You're being rude to our guest.

305
00:19:42,745 --> 00:19:45,448
Now, Ryotsu-san, please enjoy some barbecue.

306
00:19:45,648 --> 00:19:46,749
Oh, thank you.

307
00:19:47,617 --> 00:19:50,453
If you give it back now, I'll forgive you. So, hand it over.

308
00:19:50,653 --> 00:19:51,521
You're sure?

309
00:19:51,754 --> 00:19:53,623
You'll forgive me if I give it back now?

310
00:19:53,823 --> 00:19:55,758
Yes, a man keeps his word.

311
00:19:55,958 --> 00:19:56,993
What should I do?

312
00:19:57,627 --> 00:19:58,928
Please, give it back.

313
00:19:59,128 --> 00:20:02,398
Teacups like that are fragile. What if something happens to it?

314
00:20:02,632 --> 00:20:04,167
It would be too late.

315
00:20:04,367 --> 00:20:05,401
Honey.

316
00:20:06,636 --> 00:20:08,471
You're acting like a kid!

317
00:20:08,671 --> 00:20:11,474
You're stopping Ryotsu-san from having any meat.

318
00:20:12,341 --> 00:20:13,709
It's okay, Dad.

319
00:20:14,210 --> 00:20:17,213
Just lend that teacup to Ryotsu-san for a while?

320
00:20:17,580 --> 00:20:19,415
I can't do that, you idiot.

321
00:20:19,649 --> 00:20:23,185
Well, it's awful to call your daughter an idiot!

322
00:20:23,586 --> 00:20:24,987
Oh, no, I'm sorry.

323
00:20:25,254 --> 00:20:26,489
That's settled then.

324
00:20:31,494 --> 00:20:33,129
Honda-san, the meat there is done.

325
00:20:33,329 --> 00:20:35,031
Okay, I'll have some.

326
00:20:35,331 --> 00:20:39,268
Ryo-chan, why don't you eat some? It's so delicious.

327
00:20:40,670 --> 00:20:42,405
That's right. Come on, eat up.

328
00:20:42,605 --> 00:20:44,273
Reiko, you feed me.

329
00:20:44,907 --> 00:20:45,808
I refuse.

330
00:20:47,677 --> 00:20:48,911
Hey, Ryotsu.

331
00:20:49,345 --> 00:20:50,713
Come on, have a beer.

332
00:20:52,715 --> 00:20:54,183
All right, pour me some.

333
00:20:54,584 --> 00:20:57,420
That's not for drinking beer. Here you go.

334
00:20:57,620 --> 00:21:00,423
Oh, no. I couldn't dirty one of your glasses.

335
00:21:00,623 --> 00:21:02,091
Just take it.

336
00:21:04,227 --> 00:21:05,294
Come on.

337
00:21:07,830 --> 00:21:10,199
Honey, the meat's ready.

338
00:21:12,602 --> 00:21:13,569
What was that?

339
00:21:14,103 --> 00:21:15,271
What?

340
00:21:15,571 --> 00:21:19,175
Am I seeing things? I thought I saw two teacups just now.

341
00:21:19,408 --> 00:21:21,877
Are you drunk already, Chief?

342
00:21:22,078 --> 00:21:24,413
How could there be two?

343
00:21:25,848 --> 00:21:27,483
Ryotsu, show me the teacup.

344
00:21:27,717 --> 00:21:28,951
Well...

345
00:21:35,725 --> 00:21:40,463
Ryotsu, what the heck did you do to the teacup?

346
00:21:42,398 --> 00:21:46,636
I can't stand someone like you playing with my precious teacup anymore!

347
00:21:46,869 --> 00:21:48,270
Give it back right now!

348
00:21:50,139 --> 00:21:52,208
-Stay still, Ryotsu! -No way.

349
00:21:52,408 --> 00:21:53,643
Stop running!

350
00:21:55,611 --> 00:21:56,445
-I won't stop. -You idiot!

351
00:21:57,880 --> 00:21:58,648
Got you!

352
00:22:02,418 --> 00:22:03,319
Hey, Ryotsu.

353
00:22:03,519 --> 00:22:04,353
Oh no!

354
00:22:06,889 --> 00:22:09,458
M-My teacup...

355
00:22:09,659 --> 00:22:12,962
Oh dear, it broke because of the chief.

356
00:22:16,232 --> 00:22:21,504
It was my one and only treasure, my one and only!

357
00:22:22,138 --> 00:22:25,908
What am I supposed to live for from tomorrow?

358
00:22:26,709 --> 00:22:27,843
Come on, Dad.

359
00:22:28,077 --> 00:22:29,812
Don't be so depressed.

360
00:22:30,012 --> 00:22:32,014
You can buy a new one.

361
00:22:32,481 --> 00:22:33,282
Right?

362
00:22:33,949 --> 00:22:34,717
It's good.

363
00:22:34,950 --> 00:22:35,951
Ryotsu!

364
00:22:36,285 --> 00:22:39,722
What? Hurry up and eat some or I'll eat it all by myself.

365
00:22:40,122 --> 00:22:41,857
Ryo-chan, apologize properly.

366
00:22:42,091 --> 00:22:43,492
Don't you feel sorry for the chief?

367
00:22:46,295 --> 00:22:49,565
Chief, everything that has form will eventually break.

368
00:22:49,799 --> 00:22:51,500
That is the truth of all things.

369
00:22:51,701 --> 00:22:55,271
Anyway, come eat some meat. It's delicious.

370
00:22:55,471 --> 00:22:56,639
I don't want any.

371
00:22:56,839 --> 00:22:57,707
You eat it.

372
00:22:57,940 --> 00:22:59,675
All right, will do.

373
00:23:02,044 --> 00:23:03,412
Jeez, Ryo-chan!

374
00:23:03,646 --> 00:23:04,680
Chief, actually...

375
00:23:04,880 --> 00:23:06,182
No, you idiot! Don't!

376
00:23:06,382 --> 00:23:07,583
-That's what happened. -What?

377
00:23:08,050 --> 00:23:11,754
No, Chief, I just got carried away. I didn't have any bad intentions.

378
00:23:11,987 --> 00:23:15,057
Ryotsu, I won't forgive you!

379
00:23:19,328 --> 00:23:20,963
C-Chief...

380
00:23:21,430 --> 00:23:27,703
Come on, I don't taste good barbecued! Please let me go!

381
00:23:27,903 --> 00:23:29,605
It's hot! It's hot!

382
00:23:29,839 --> 00:23:32,341
Ryo-chan got what he deserved.

383
00:23:32,541 --> 00:23:35,344
This turned out to be quite a birthday, Hiromi-san.

384
00:23:35,544 --> 00:23:38,180
But my dad seems to be having a lot of fun.

385
00:23:38,381 --> 00:23:40,316
Charcoal-grilled Ryotsu.

386
00:23:41,050 --> 00:23:42,685
Hot! It's hot!

387
00:23:42,885 --> 00:23:45,388
This is the best present for me.

388
00:23:45,588 --> 00:23:47,256
Chief, please spare me!

389
00:23:47,456 --> 00:23:51,560
Nakagawa, Reiko, Honda, Hiromi-san, help me!

390
00:23:55,464 --> 00:23:57,099
TODAY'S DAMAGE REPORT

391
00:23:57,333 --> 00:24:02,071
ONE KURORAKU-JAWAN
